  <!-- INTRO PROSE -->
  <section class="about-intro">
    <div class="section-label">Who I Am</div>
    <div class="about-intro__body">
      <p>
        I'm a product designer and design technologist. I've spent over <strong>26 years</strong>
        making digital products that hold their shape under pressure — functional, considered,
        and worth looking at twice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I'm a <strong>Senior Designer at Booz Allen Hamilton</strong>, currently embedded
        with the USPS as a Senior Product Designer. Before that, I spent years as Digital Director
        at <strong>Catholic Relief Services</strong> — one of the world's largest humanitarian aid
        organizations — where I built and led the team responsible for front and back-end development,
        online fundraising, UX, information architecture, and email marketing.
      </p>
      <p>
        But design, for me, started long before screens. It started with my hands. I've been making
        things since I was a teenager — first leather goods, then pottery. I spent <strong>19 years
        making and selling functional stoneware</strong> at the American Crafts Marketplace. That
        time taught me something I've never been able to unlearn: good design is felt before it's
        understood.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I'm not designing, I'm in the kitchen — baking sourdough, cooking without a recipe,
        and generally treating food the same way I treat design work: with patience and an unreasonable
        amount of attention to detail.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

